    "old": "<img src=\"https://itsdrdan.github.io/textbook/figures/pathways/oer/cac_wheel.svg\" alt=\"The citric acid cycle as a wheel of structures. Step 1, citrate synthase: acetyl CoA (2 carbons) and water join oxaloacetate to make citrate, releasing CoA-SH. Step 2, aconitase: citrate is rearranged to isocitrate. Step 3, isocitrate dehydrogenase: NAD+ is reduced to NADH and CO2 leaves, giving alpha-ketoglutarate. Step 4, alpha-ketoglutarate dehydrogenase: NAD+ is reduced to NADH and CO2 leaves, giving succinyl CoA. Step 5, succinyl CoA synthetase: GDP and phosphate make GTP, giving succinate. Step 6, succinate dehydrogenase: FAD is reduced to FADH2, giving fumarate. Step 7, fumarase: water adds, giving malate. Step 8, malate dehydrogenase: NAD+ is reduced to NADH, regenerating oxaloacetate. Per turn: 2 CO2, 3 NADH, 1 FADH2 and 1 GTP.\" style=\"width:760px;max-width:100%;height:auto\" />",
    "new": "<img width=\"760\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;\" alt=\"The citric acid cycle as a loop. Step 1, citrate synthase: acetyl CoA (2 carbons) and water join oxaloacetate (4 carbons) to make citrate (6 carbons), releasing CoA-SH. Step 2, aconitase: citrate is rearranged to isocitrate. Step 3, isocitrate dehydrogenase: NAD+ is reduced to NADH and CO2 leaves, giving alpha-ketoglutarate (5 carbons). Step 4, alpha-ketoglutarate dehydrogenase: NAD+ is reduced to NADH and CO2 leaves, giving succinyl CoA (4 carbons). Step 5, succinyl CoA synthetase: GDP and phosphate make GTP, giving succinate. Step 6, succinate dehydrogenase: FAD is reduced to FADH2, giving fumarate. Step 7, fumarase: water adds, giving malate. Step 8, malate dehydrogenase: NAD+ is reduced to NADH, regenerating oxaloacetate. Per turn: 2 CO2, 3 NADH, 1 FADH2 and 1 GTP.\" src=\"/@api/deki/files/{{cac}}/fig-p597202-cac-flow.svg\" fileid=\"{{cac}}\" />",
    "count": 1,
    "note": "14.3.1 citric acid cycle as a landscape loop (the wheel printed at ~2 pt)"
   }
